Refactor Plan

Phase A: Define the final signing model

ADMIN wallet signs token mint creation
MAKER wallet signs mint-request creation and transfer-request creation
CHECKER wallet signs approve/reject actions that must touch chain
backend becomes workflow coordinator, validator, and recorder
Decision boundary:

off-chain approval/rejection can stay in DB if you want business approval before chain action
on-chain request creation/approval should be browser-signed where the program expects those role signers


Phase B: Refactor backend to be transaction-preparation first

stop assuming backend maker/checker signers for normal request execution
add prepare endpoints for:
admin mint creation
maker mint request creation
maker transfer request creation
checker on-chain approval
checker on-chain rejection if you want rejection reflected on chain too
keep backend endpoints for:
request CRUD
role checks
status transitions
audit logs
result recording


Phase C: Make mint browser-signed

add browser transaction builder for create_mint_request
allow maker Phantom wallet to initiate mint requests just like transfer/burn
record request PDA, source/destination token accounts, signature, explorer URL
This is the biggest current gap.


Phase D: Make admin token creation browser-signed


replace backend-only token mint creation with admin-wallet signing from the Solana admin page
backend should only persist the created mint after the wallet transaction succeeds


Phase E: Unify checker flow

checker approves/rejects business workflow in the portal
if approved and chain action is required, checker Phantom signs the on-chain approval
backend records final tx result and marks request executed
remove dependence on SOLANA_CHECKER_KEYPAIR_PATH for standard operator flows


Phase F: Simplify statuses
Recommended final status model:

DRAFT
PENDING_APPROVAL
REJECTED
APPROVED
ON_CHAIN_PENDING
EXECUTED
FAILED
Or keep current names and map them cleanly:

checker approval immediately makes request executable
wallet signing updates on-chain metadata
final chain confirmation moves to EXECUTED

Phase G: UI cleanup

role-specific action buttons only
wallet mismatch warnings for admin/maker/checker
hide backend execution buttons when browser signing is the intended path
show exact next actor:
